"""Source-authored bilingual manuscript. Review scope: depth-review-2026-10-20/REPORT.md."""
from model import p, ref, block, section

PART = dict(title=p('《打擊洗錢及恐怖分子資金籌集條例》：附表', 'Anti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorist Financing Ordinance: schedules'),
intro=p('先記住定義及法定最低要求，再到第6部分掌握指引下的完整操作。門檻、額外措施及例外均須連同適用對象理解。', 'Learn the definitions and statutory minimum requirements, then use Part 6 for full operational guidance. Read thresholds, additional measures and exceptions together with their applicable persons.'), sections=[
section('definitions', '附表1及附表2：重要定義', 'Schedules 1 and 2: key definitions', [
    block('金融機構、關係及對等司法管轄區', 'Institutions, relationships and equivalent jurisdictions', [
        ('「金融機構」在附表裡是一張法定類別清單，而且不是每一類都用同一套發牌部。它涵蓋認可機構、持牌法團、獲授權保險人、持牌個人保險代理／保險代理機構／保險經紀公司、金錢服務經營者、郵政署署長、儲值支付工具持牌人、持牌虛擬資產服務提供者及穩定幣持牌人等法定類別。各類別並非適用完全相同的發牌部份。', 'In the Schedules, “financial institution” is a statutory list of categories, and they do not all use the same licensing Part. Financial institutions include authorized institutions, licensed corporations, authorized insurers, licensed individual insurance agents, agencies or broker companies, MSOs, the Postmaster General, SVF licensees, licensed VAS providers and stablecoin licensees. They do not all use the same licensing Part.'),
        ('「業務關係」和「非經常交易」要分開記，金額小並不會自動把已經存在的持續關係取消。業務關係是有持續性元素的業務、專業或商業關係；或者，機構在對方首次以準客戶身分接觸時，便預期會有這種持續性元素（兩者擇一）。非經常交易，是機構與沒有業務關係的客戶之間的交易。例如：一名顧客每星期都來兌換，機構一開始已預期會持續往來，這已經是業務關係。後來某一天他只換了一小筆錢，並不會因此變成「沒有業務關係的非經常交易」。', 'A “business relationship” and an “occasional transaction” are different things. A small amount does not, by itself, cancel an ongoing relationship that already exists. A business relationship is a business, professional or commercial relationship with an element of duration, or one expected to have that element when the person first contacts the institution as a potential customer (either will do). An occasional transaction is with a customer who has no business relationship. For example: a customer comes in to exchange currency every week, and the institution expected an ongoing relationship from the first contact. That is already a business relationship. The fact that one later visit is only for a small amount does not turn it into an occasional transaction with no business relationship.'),
        ('「對等司法管轄區」和「營業日」都有法定定義，不要用日常口語來替代。對等司法管轄區指香港以外的 FATF 成員，或採取與附表2相若要求的司法管轄區。「營業日」的法定定義排除公眾假期、烈風警告日及黑色暴雨警告日；遇到以營業日計算的期限，必須使用這個法定定義。', '“Equivalent jurisdiction” and “business day” both have statutory definitions, and everyday language should not be substituted for them. An equivalent jurisdiction is a FATF member other than Hong Kong, or a jurisdiction imposing requirements similar to Schedule 2. The statutory business-day definition excludes public holidays, gale-warning days and black-rainstorm-warning days. Apply that definition wherever a deadline is counted in business days.'),
    ], [
        ref('04', '附表1第1–3條；附表2第1條', 'Schedule 1 ss.1–3; Schedule 2 s.1', 'equivalent jurisdiction'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('實益擁有人與政治人物', 'Beneficial owners and PEPs', [
        ('客戶的實益擁有人，門檻同樣是「超過25%」，剛好25%並未達到這個百分比測試；但即使未過百分比，仍須檢查是否有控制權。公司：自然人直接或間接擁有或控制超過25%已發行股本，或行使或控制超過25%股東大會投票權，或最終控制管理。合夥：自然人直接或間接超過25%資本、利潤或投票權，或最終控制管理。兩類也都包括交易為其進行的另一「人」，不能把這個分支一概限於自然人。例如：某人剛好持有25%已發行股本，沒有超過門檻，但仍可能因為最終控制管理，或因為交易是為另一「人」進行，而被識別為實益擁有人。', 'A customer’s beneficial owner is also identified using a “more than 25%” threshold. Exactly 25% misses that percentage test, but control must still be examined. For corporations: individuals directly or indirectly owning or controlling more than 25% of issued capital or general-meeting votes, or exercising ultimate management control. For partnerships: individuals with, directly or indirectly, more than 25% of capital, profits or votes, or ultimate management control. Both also include another “person” on whose behalf the transaction is conducted; that limb is not universally limited to individuals. For example: a person who holds exactly 25% of issued capital misses the percentage threshold, but may still be a beneficial owner through ultimate management control, or because the transaction is conducted for another “person”.'),
        ('信託的實益擁有人，範圍比「點名的個人受益人」更廣，不能漏掉類別受益人，也不能把受益人一律限成個人。信託實益擁有人包括：有權享有信託財產既得權益的受益人，或某類別受益人（不論是管有權、剩餘權或復歸權，亦不論可否廢除）；財產授予人；受託人；保護人或執行人；或最終控制該信託的自然人。對公司、合夥、信託以外的人，附表2第1條涵蓋最終擁有或控制的自然人，或該人代其行事的另一人。例如：一份信託寫的是「某家族的子女」這一類受益人，而不是逐一點名，這些類別受益人仍屬實益擁有人，不能因為未列出個人姓名就略過。', 'The beneficial owners of a trust are wider than “named individual beneficiaries”. Do not omit a class of beneficiaries, and do not limit beneficiaries to individuals. Trust BOs include a beneficiary or class of beneficiaries entitled to a vested interest in trust property, whether in possession, remainder or reversion and whether defeasible or not; the settlor; trustee; protector/enforcer; or an individual with ultimate control. For a person other than a corporation, partnership or trust, section 1 covers an individual ultimately owning or controlling it, or another person on whose behalf it acts. For example: a trust that refers to “the children of a family” as a class, without naming each child, still has those class beneficiaries as beneficial owners. They must not be skipped merely because no individual names are listed.'),
        ('條例本身所說的政治人物（PEP），針對的是在香港以外擔任重要公職的人；香港本地及國際組織政治人物，是指引另行處理的。法定名單包括國家或政府首長、高級政客、政府／司法／軍事高層、國企高級行政人員及重要政黨幹事，亦包括法定家庭成員及密切聯繫者；但不包括中級或初級職員。例如：一名外國部長的配偶，可以落入法定 PEP 範圍；一名本地區議員則不是這條法定定義下的 PEP，而要看指引對香港本地政治人物的處理。', 'The Ordinance’s own PEP definition concerns people who hold prominent public functions outside Hong Kong. Domestic Hong Kong PEPs, and international-organisation PEPs, are addressed separately in the Guideline. The statutory PEP definition includes heads of state or government, senior politicians, senior government, judicial or military officials, senior executives of state enterprises and important political-party officials, plus statutory family members and close associates. It excludes middle or junior officials. For example: the spouse of a foreign minister can fall within the statutory PEP definition. A local district councillor is not a PEP under this statutory definition, and is instead considered under the Guideline’s treatment of domestic PEPs.'),
    ], [
        ref('04', '附表2第1條', 'Schedule 2 s.1', 'more than 25%'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('公共機構及識別文件', 'Public bodies and identification documents', [
        ('「公共機構」比「政府部門」更廣，法人的定義也包含這些機構。公共機構包括行政、立法、市政議會，政府部門或事業，地方或公共當局或事業，由行政長官或政府委任的委員會等組織，以及依法可以用公共身分行事的組織。法人包括公共機構，以及有或沒有法團身分的團體。', 'A “public body” is wider than a government department, and the definition of a legal person includes these bodies. Public bodies include executive, legislative or municipal or urban councils; government departments or undertakings; local or public authorities or undertakings; boards appointed by the Chief Executive or the Government; and bodies empowered by enactment to act in a public capacity. Legal persons include public bodies and incorporated or unincorporated bodies.'),
        ('條例按不同類型的人，列明什麼才是法定識別文件，不要把這個清單與指引裡較寬的核實來源混為一談。附表2法定識別文件：自然人為身分證、身分證明書、簽證身分書或旅行證件；香港公司為成立證明或遷冊證明；註冊非香港公司為相關註冊證明。其他境外法團，則用當地相當註冊機關發出的成立、註冊或等同證明。', 'The Ordinance lists particular identification documents for particular types of person. That list is not the same as the Guideline’s wider verification sources. Schedule 2 statutory identification documents: individuals—identity card, certificate/document of identity or travel document; Hong Kong companies—incorporation or re-domiciliation certificate; registered non-Hong Kong companies—registration certificate; other foreign corporations—incorporation/registration or equivalent evidence from the corresponding local authority.'),
        ('合夥要用哪一份法定識別文件，先看它是否在香港經營。在港經營的合夥，法定識別文件是商業登記證；不在港經營的合夥，則是合夥協議，或政府發出的成立或註冊文件。必須分清這個定義，與指引一般可採用的可靠獨立核實資料，並不是同一個清單。', 'Which statutory identification document a partnership needs depends on whether it carries on business in Hong Kong. For a Hong Kong-business partnership, the statutory identification document is the business registration certificate. For a partnership not doing business in Hong Kong, it is the partnership agreement, or government formation or registration evidence. This definition is not the same list as the Guideline’s wider reliable and independent verification sources.'),
    ], [
        ref('04', '附表2第1條', 'Schedule 2 s.1', 'public body'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('金融機構以外的指定行業及數碼識別', 'Designated non-financial professions and digital identification', [
        ('DNFBP 是「指定非金融業人士」的縮寫，不是所有非金融商戶，也不等於金錢服務經營者。它包括會計專業人士、地產代理、法律專業人士、信託或公司服務（TCSP）持牌人，以及貴金屬及寶石 B 類註冊人。例如：一間普通零售店或一間金錢服務經營者，都不會只因為「不是銀行」，就自動變成 DNFBP。', 'DNFBP means designated non-financial businesses and professions. It does not mean every non-financial business, and it is not another name for an MSO. The category covers accounting professionals, estate agents, legal professionals, trust or company service provider (TCSP) licensees, and Category B precious-metals and stones registrants. For example: an ordinary retail shop, or an MSO, does not become a DNFBP merely because it is “not a bank”.'),
        ('「認可數碼識別系統」有法定門檻，不是任何電子或視像核對都可以算。它必須是由相應有關當局或監管機構認可的可靠獨立來源。對金錢服務經營者來說，認可當局是海關關長。使用數碼文件、視像通話或一般手機驗證，本身並不等於使用了這個法定認可系統。例如：職員用手機視像看一看顧客的身分證，即使得以核對面貌，也不因此就變成已經使用「認可數碼識別系統」。', 'A “recognized digital identification system” has a statutory threshold. Not every electronic or video check qualifies. It must be a reliable independent source recognized by the applicable authority or regulatory body. For an MSO, the recognizing authority is the CCE. Electronic files, a video call, or ordinary mobile verification do not, by themselves, constitute a statutory recognized system. For example: a staff member who views a customer’s identity card over a phone video call is not, for that reason alone, using a recognized digital identification system.'),
    ], [
        ref('04', '附表1第2部第1條；附表2第1條', 'Schedule 1 Part 2 s.1; Schedule 2 s.1', 'DNFBP (指定非金融業人士)'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('對等司法管轄區的評估不是只記名單', 'Assessing equivalent jurisdictions beyond a memorised list', [
        ('對不是 FATF 成員的司法管轄區，金錢服務經營者可能要自己判斷它是否有相類規定，並且把評估記錄下來，而不是只背一份現成名單。可以考慮的因素包括：FATF 類區域組織的成員資格或相互評估、策略缺失及改善進度、關長通函，以及專門機構刊物。評估須定期覆核，或在觸發事件後覆核。', 'For a jurisdiction that is not a FATF member, an MSO may need to decide for itself whether comparable requirements apply, and to document that assessment, rather than only memorising a ready-made list. Factors that may be considered include FATF-style regional membership or mutual evaluations, strategic deficiencies and progress, CCE advisories, and specialist publications. The assessment should be reviewed regularly, and also after trigger events.'),
    ], [
        ref('03', '第4.16.2–4.16.3段', '¶4.16.2–4.16.3', 'The MSO should document its assessment of the jurisdiction'),
    ], kind='list'),
]),
section('core-duties', '四項盡職審查與觸發條件', 'Four CDD measures and their triggers', [
    block('須認識：核實客戶身分的五類法定來源', 'Recognise: five statutory sources for customer identity verification', [
        ('核實客戶身分時，條例給出五類可以擇一使用的法定來源，不是只能用一種紙本證件，也不是任何「看起來可信」的資料都自動合格。這五類是：(1) 政府機構；(2) 有關當局或任何其他有關主管當局；(3) 在香港以外執行相類職能的主管當局；(4) 認可數碼識別系統；(5) 有關當局認可的任何其他可靠及獨立來源。可採用來自這些來源的文件、數據或資料。對應：附表2 section 2(1)(a)。', 'When verifying a customer’s identity, the Ordinance gives five statutory sources that may be used as alternatives. The rule is not limited to one paper identity document, and not every apparently credible source automatically qualifies. Schedule 2 section 2(1)(a) provides five alternative sources (OR): (1) a governmental body; (2) the relevant authority or any other relevant authority; (3) an overseas authority performing similar functions; (4) a recognized digital identification system; or (5) any other reliable and independent source recognized by the relevant authority. Documents, data or information from these sources may be used.'),
        ('適用於金錢服務經營者的「認可」，是海關關長作出的認可。還要分清另一份清單：就代表客戶行事的人，section 2(1)(d)(i) 明列的是四類——政府、相關當局、境外相類當局，以及認可的其他可靠獨立來源；這份清單沒有另外列出「認可數碼識別系統」一項。核實代表本人的身分，與核實其代表客戶行事的授權，仍然是兩項工作。', 'For an MSO, “recognition” means recognition by the CCE. A different list also has to be kept distinct. For a person acting for a customer, section 2(1)(d)(i) expressly lists four categories: governmental bodies, relevant authorities, similar overseas authorities, and recognized other reliable independent sources. It does not separately list a recognized digital identification system. Verifying the representative’s identity, and verifying that person’s authority to act, remain separate tasks.'),
    ], [
        ref('04', '附表2第1條「認可數碼識別系統」、第2(1)(a)、(d)(i)–(ii)條', 'Schedule 2 s.1 “recognized digital identification system”; s.2(1)(a), (d)(i)–(ii)', 'a governmental body'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('完整措施及時間', 'Full measures and timing', [
        ('法定的客戶盡職審查有四項措施，而且「識別」和「核實」是兩項不同工作。這四項是：識別及核實客戶；識別實益擁有人，並採取合理措施核實他們，以及了解法人或信託的結構；取得業務關係目的及擬具有的性質的資料（除非已經明顯可見）；以及識別並核實代表客戶行事的人，及其授權。', 'Statutory customer due diligence consists of four measures, and identification is a different task from verification. The four CDD measures are: identify and verify the customer; identify beneficial owners and take reasonable measures to verify them, understanding the structure of a legal person or trust; obtain information on the purpose and intended nature of the relationship, unless that is obvious; and identify and verify persons acting for the customer, and their authority.'),
        ('什麼時候必須先做盡職審查，要連同金額門檻和「有關連交易」一起記。必須在建立業務關係之前進行；在一般非經常交易等於或超過港幣120,000元之前進行；以及在金融機構的非經常電傳轉賬或虛擬資產轉移等於或超過港幣8,000元之前進行。單次操作，或看似有關連的多次操作，都須合併考慮。持牌虛擬資產服務提供者另外有一項「非轉賬非經常交易 8,000元」的規則，不能把它當成所有金錢服務經營者的一般門檻。例如：同一名沒有業務關係的顧客，同一天分幾筆兌換，合計達到港幣120,000元，便可能因為看似有關連而觸發盡職審查，不能只看每一筆都低於門檻。', 'When CDD must be completed is a timing rule, and it has to be read together with the amount thresholds and with linked operations. CDD precedes a business relationship, general occasional transactions of at least HK$120,000, and financial-institution occasional wire or VA transfers of at least HK$8,000. A single operation, or apparently linked operations, must be considered together. Licensed VAS providers have a separate HK$8,000 rule for non-transfer occasional transactions; that is not every MSO’s general threshold. For example: a customer with no business relationship makes several exchanges on the same day that together reach HK$120,000. If the operations appear linked, CDD may be triggered even though each individual amount is below the threshold.'),
        ('如果懷疑涉及洗錢或恐怖分子資金籌集，或懷疑以往識別或核實資料是否真確、是否足夠，同樣必須做盡職審查，不受上面那些金額門檻限制。另外，非電傳匯款若達港幣8,000元，還有一套獨立的識別及紀錄責任。例如：顧客只兌換港幣3萬元，但職員已經懷疑資金與洗錢有關，仍必須做盡職審查，不能因為未達12萬元就略過。對應：附表2 section 13（非電傳匯款達港幣8,000元的特定識別及紀錄責任）。', 'Suspicion, or doubt about earlier identification or verification information, also requires CDD, and those amount thresholds do not stand in the way. Suspicion of ML or TF, or doubt about previous identification or verification information, also triggers CDD, regardless of those thresholds. Section 13 separately imposes specified identification and record duties for non-wire remittance of at least HK$8,000. For example: a customer is only exchanging HK$30,000, but staff already suspect the funds may be connected with money laundering. CDD is still required. The fact that the amount is below HK$120,000 does not allow it to be skipped.'),
        ('核實身分，原則上應在建立關係前完成；只有在很窄的條件下，才可以延後。延後核實只可在「不打斷正常業務所必需」，而且風險能夠有效受管理時使用，並且必須在關係建立後，在合理切實可行的範圍內盡快完成。如果不能遵從，便不得建立關係或進行非經常交易；已經建立的關係，須盡快終止。例如：不能只因為客人趕時間，就一律把核實留到「以後再補」。必須同時符合「不打斷正常業務所必需」和「風險已有效管理」，並且盡快補做；補不到，就要停止業務往來。', 'Identity verification should, as a rule, be completed before a relationship is established. It may be deferred only in a narrow case. Delayed verification requires necessity to avoid interrupting normal business and effective risk management; complete it as soon as reasonably practicable after establishment. If the institution is unable to comply, it must not establish the relationship or carry out the occasional transaction; an existing relationship must be terminated promptly. For example: a customer being in a hurry is not, by itself, a reason to leave verification until later. Both “necessary to avoid interrupting normal business” and effective risk management must be present, and the verification must be completed promptly. If it cannot be completed, the business must not go ahead, or must be ended.'),
    ], [
        ref('04', '附表2第2–3、13條', 'Schedule 2 ss.2–3, 13', 'before establishing a business relationship with the customer'),
    ], kind='list'),
]),
section('simplification', '簡化審查：只豁免指定措施', 'Simplified CDD: only specified measures are omitted', [
    block('簡化審查只豁免哪些指定措施', 'Scope of simplified CDD under section 4', [
        ('簡化盡職審查（SDD）並不是「甚麼都不用做」，它只豁免指定的實益擁有人措施。當有合理理由相信客戶屬於合資格類別時，可以不做 section 2(1)(b) 的實益擁有人措施；其餘關於客戶、代表人，以及目的或性質的措施仍然適用。如果合資格實體出現在擁有權鏈之內，豁免只及於該實體及其以上的部分，不是整條鏈都可以不再查。例如：客戶是一間合資格的上市法團，你可以省略對該客戶本身的實益擁有人措施，但仍須識別及核實客戶、代表人，並了解業務目的。若上市法團只是中間的一層，豁免停在該層，不能自動把更下層的擁有權也全部略過。對應：附表2 section 4。', 'Simplified due diligence (SDD) is not a licence to skip CDD altogether. Only a specified beneficial-owner measure may be omitted. Where there are reasonable grounds that the customer qualifies, section 2(1)(b) beneficial-owner measures may be omitted; the measures concerning the customer, the representative, and the purpose or nature of the relationship still apply. If a qualifying entity appears in an ownership chain, the exemption stops at or beyond that entity; it does not run throughout the whole chain. For example: if the customer is a qualifying listed corporation, the beneficial-owner measures as regards that customer may be omitted, but you must still identify and verify the customer and any representative, and obtain the purpose of the relationship. If the listed corporation is only an intermediate layer, the exemption stops there and does not automatically waive the rest of the chain below it.'),
        ('哪些客戶可以考慮簡化審查，要記法定類別，不要自行擴大。合資格類別：金融機構；在對等司法管轄區成立、經營相若金融業務、有相若措施且受相類當局監管的機構；在任何證券市場上市的法團；合資格投資公司；香港政府或公共機構；以及對等司法管轄區的政府或相若公共機構。投資公司還有額外條件：全部投資者都必須已由以下人士做相類盡職審查：金融機構；或者在香港或對等司法管轄區成立、有相類合規措施並受遵從監管的機構。', 'Which customers may be considered for simplified CDD is a statutory list, and it should not be widened informally. Qualifying categories: financial institutions; equivalent-jurisdiction institutions with similar financial business, similar compliance measures and comparable-authority supervision; corporations listed on any stock market; qualifying investment companies; Hong Kong Government/public bodies; and equivalent-jurisdiction governments/similar bodies. For an investment company, all investors must receive similar CDD from an FI, or from an institution established in Hong Kong or an equivalent jurisdiction with similar compliance measures and supervision for compliance.'),
        ('另外還有幾類指定產品例外，它們不是一般匯款的「免審查門檻」。包括：供款從受僱收入扣除、而且權益不可轉讓的僱員退休計劃；沒有退保條款、且不可作抵押的相關計劃保單；以及每年保費不多於港幣8,000元，或單次保費不多於港幣20,000元的人壽保單。例如：一筆普通的港幣8,000元匯款，不能因為人壽保單有一個8,000元的年保費數字，就被當成同樣獲得簡化或豁免。', 'There are also a few specified product exceptions. They are not a general remittance threshold below which CDD can be skipped. Product exceptions cover employee retirement schemes funded by employment-income deductions with non-assignable interests; relevant scheme insurance without a surrender value or use as collateral; and life policies with an annual premium of no more than HK$8,000, or a single premium of no more than HK$20,000. For example: an ordinary remittance of HK$8,000 does not become simplified or exempt merely because a life policy has an HK$8,000 annual-premium figure.'),
        ('律師或律師行的客戶帳戶要享受實益擁有人措施例外，必須同時符合全部指定條件，不是只要戶口名稱裡有律師行便可以。該帳戶須以其名義開立、混合其客戶的金錢或證券，並且由其作為代理管理，才適用 section 4(6) 的例外。一旦出現懷疑，或對資料有疑問，仍須按 section 3 處理。例如：一間律師行只是用自己名義開了一個普通辦事處戶口，並沒有混合客戶金錢、也不是作為代理管理客戶資金，便不符合這項例外。', 'A solicitor’s or law firm’s client account qualifies for the beneficial-owner measure exception only if all of the specified conditions are met. It is not enough that the account name contains a law firm. For solicitor/firm accounts, section 4(6) requires the account to be in the solicitor’s/firm’s name, mix clients’ money/securities, and be managed as their agent. Suspicion, or doubts about the information, still require handling under section 3. For example: a law firm’s ordinary office account in its own name, which does not mix client money and is not managed as agent for clients, does not meet this exception.'),
    ], [
        ref('04', '附表2第3–4條', 'Schedule 2 ss.3–4', 'Simplified customer due diligence'),
    ], kind='list'),
]),
section('special-cases', '額外措施：遙距、政治人物及其他高風險', 'Additional measures: remote customers, PEPs and other high risk', [
    block('先完成普通CDD，再加所需措施', 'Additional to ordinary CDD', [
        ('客戶不是親身出示身分時，普通盡職審查之後，還須至少再加一項指定措施；不是所有視像或電子程序都可以替代。可以擇一的措施是：用未曾使用過的 section 2(1)(a) 或 (ab) 資料再核實；對已取得的資料作補充核實；或確保付款（若有多筆，則為第一筆）經由客戶同名戶口進行。該戶口必須設在認可機構；或設在同時符合四項條件的境外機構：在對等司法管轄區成立、經營相若銀行業務、有相類合規措施，並受當地相當於金管局的主管當局監管。如果客戶已按認可數碼識別系統的資料，完成 section 2(1)(a) 或 (ab) 的措施，才有 section 9(2) 的例外。例如：只是用視像看一看顧客持有身分證，並不符合這項認可數碼識別系統例外；仍須在上述三項額外措施之中至少完成一項。', 'If the customer is not identified face to face, ordinary CDD is not the end of the matter. At least one extra specified measure is required, and not every video or electronic process is a substitute. Non-face-to-face identification requires at least one: further verification with previously unused section 2(1)(a)/(ab) material; supplementary verification of obtained information; or payment (the first if multiple) through the customer’s same-name account. That account must be at an authorized institution, or at an overseas institution meeting all four conditions: establishment in an equivalent jurisdiction, similar banking business, similar compliance measures, and supervision by a local authority with HKMA-like functions. Section 9(2) excepts customers whose section 2(1)(a) or (ab) measures use a recognized digital identification system, not every video or electronic process. For example: watching a customer hold up an identity card on a video call does not meet this recognized-digital-ID exception. At least one of the three extra measures above is still required.'),
        ('非香港政治人物的關係，必須先得到高級管理層批准，並且合理確立財富來源和資金來源，才能建立或繼續；不能只因為對方已經離任，或過了某個固定年數，就自動豁免。前政治人物只有在經過適當風險評估、認定不再屬高風險時，才可以使用法定例外。例如：一名五年前卸任的外國部長要開立業務關係，不能只算「已經離任五年」便當成例外。必須先做適當評估，並且確認不再屬高風險，才可使用該例外；否則仍須高級管理層批准，並合理確立財富及資金來源。', 'A relationship with a non-Hong Kong PEP cannot be established or continued just because the person has left office, or because a fixed number of years has passed. Non-Hong Kong PEP relationships require senior-management approval and reasonable establishment of both wealth and funds sources before establishment or continuation. A former PEP qualifies for the statutory exception only after an appropriate assessment establishes that the person is no longer high-risk, not automatically after leaving office or after a fixed number of years. For example: a foreign minister who left office five years ago and now wants a business relationship is not excepted merely because five years have passed. An appropriate assessment must first establish that the person is no longer high-risk. Otherwise, senior-management approval and reasonable establishment of the sources of wealth and funds are still required.'),
        ('其他高風險情況的額外措施，與政治人物的整套指定措施並不相同，管理層批准也不是可有可無的選項。就這些情況，建立或繼續關係必須先得到高級管理層批准，然後再合理確立財富及資金來源，或採取其他額外緩解措施；如果是現有關係，還須合理核實實益擁有人。非經常交易則須採取額外緩解措施。這項「來源或其他緩解」的選擇，不能用來取代政治人物的全部指定措施。對應：附表2 section 15（其他高風險情況）。', 'The extra measures for other high-risk cases are not the same as the full set of PEP measures, and senior-management approval is not optional. For section 15 other high-risk cases, establishing/continuing a relationship requires senior approval plus either reasonable establishment of wealth/funds sources or other additional mitigation; existing relationships also require reasonable BO verification. Occasional transactions require additional mitigation. Approval is not optional, and this choice does not replace all PEP measures.'),
        ('不得開立或維持匿名帳戶，也不得開立或維持以虛假姓名開立的帳戶。認可機構不得與 section 17 所界定的空殼銀行法團，建立或繼續往來銀行關係。', 'Do not open or maintain anonymous accounts, or accounts in a fictitious name. Authorized institutions must not establish or continue correspondent relationships with shell-bank corporations as defined in section 17.'),
    ], [
        ref('04', '附表2第8–10、15–17條', 'Schedule 2 ss.8–10, 15–17', 'at least one of the following measures'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('空殼銀行：四項條件與實體經營', 'Shell banks: cumulative conditions and physical presence', [
        ('空殼銀行不是「所有境外銀行」或「沒有香港分行的銀行」的另一個名稱。section 17 禁止認可機構與之建立或繼續代理銀行關係的對象，必須同時符合四項：(1) 在香港以外註冊成立；(2) 獲當地授權經營銀行業務；(3) 在當地沒有實體經營；(4) 並非在某司法管轄區註冊、獲授權且有實體經營的銀行法團的聯屬公司。例如：一間在海外註冊、在當地有辦事處和全職銀行職員的網上銀行，即使沒有香港分行，也不會只因此自動變成這條所說的空殼銀行。', 'A “shell bank” is not simply another name for every overseas bank, or every bank without a Hong Kong branch. The section 17 correspondent prohibition for authorized institutions concerns a corporation that cumulatively is (1) incorporated outside Hong Kong, (2) authorized there to conduct banking, (3) without physical presence there, and (4) not affiliated with a corporation that is incorporated, authorized to conduct banking, and physically present in a jurisdiction. For example: an internet bank incorporated overseas, with premises and full-time banking staff in that place, is not automatically a shell bank under this section merely because it has no Hong Kong branch.'),
        ('「實體經營」和「聯屬」也有定義。實體經營是指在當地處所經營銀行業務，並且至少有一名全職僱員在該處履行銀行職務。聯屬包括附屬公司，或至少有一名自然人同時是兩家法團的控制人的法定情況。這條的直接責任人是認可機構，不是把金錢服務經營者當成提供代理銀行服務的銀行。', '“Physical presence” and “affiliation” also have definitions. Physical presence requires that banking is carried on at premises there, and that at least one full-time employee performs banking duties there. Affiliation includes subsidiary status, or the statutory case in which at least one individual is simultaneously a controller of both corporations. The direct section 17 duty is on authorized institutions. It is not a rule that treats an MSO as a correspondent bank.'),
    ], [
        ref('04', '附表2第17(1)–(3)條', 'Schedule 2 s.17(1)–(3)', 'Correspondent banking relationships with shell banks'),
    ], kind='list'),
]),
section('sector-specific', '其他金融機構的特定要求', 'Specific requirements for other financial activities', [
    block('保單、往來銀行及虛擬資產', 'Insurance, correspondent banking and virtual assets', [
        ('保單受益人的識別，時間點很重要：指定時先記錄，真正核實則最遲在行使既得權利或首次付款兩者較早的時間完成。指定時，若已有姓名便記錄姓名；若是以類別或描述指定，則取得足夠資料，確保屆時能夠確立身分。到了該較早時間，須核實受益人；若受益人是法人或信託，還須識別實益擁有人，並在高風險時採取合理措施核實他們。', 'When an insurance beneficiary is identified matters. Record the designation first; verification is due by the earlier of the exercise of vested rights and the first payout. When the beneficiary is designated, record the name, or, if the beneficiary is described as a class or by description, obtain enough information to establish identity by that earlier time. Verify then. If the beneficiary is a legal person or a trust, identify the beneficial owners and reasonably verify them where the risk is high.'),
        ('認可機構與境外對手建立往來銀行關係之前，有一套額外要求，不是開了戶口再補做。須先了解對方的業務、聲譽及監管情況，以及其打擊洗錢制度；取得高級管理層批准；信納其制度足夠而且有效；並記錄雙方責任。如果對手的客戶可以直接使用該帳戶（payable-through），還須符合對方已做盡職審查及監察、以及可以提供資料等條件。', 'Before an authorized institution establishes a correspondent relationship with an overseas respondent, extra steps are required. They are not something to be completed after the account is already open. The institution must understand the respondent’s business, reputation and supervision, and its AML controls; obtain senior-management approval; satisfy itself that the controls are adequate and effective; and document the responsibilities of each side. If the respondent’s customers can use the account directly (payable-through), the respondent’s CDD and monitoring, and access to the relevant data, are also required.'),
        ('虛擬資產轉移也有一套「誰要記錄什麼」的規則，金額是否達到港幣8,000元會影響要附加的資料。它是指代匯款人把虛擬資產轉至受款人在受款機構的安排。匯款機構須記錄並提交匯款人及受款人的姓名，以及帳戶或參考編號；達到港幣8,000元時，還要加上匯款人地址、客戶或識別文件號碼，或出生日期及地點，其中一項。受款機構須記錄收到的資料；中介機構則須傳遞全部收到的資料。', 'A virtual-asset transfer has its own rules on who must record what, and the HK$8,000 threshold affects the extra originator information. A VA transfer moves virtual assets for an originator to a recipient at a beneficiary institution. The ordering institution records and submits both names and the account or reference identifiers. At HK$8,000, it must also add one of: the originator’s address, a customer or document identifier, or the date and place of birth. Beneficiary institutions record the information received. Intermediaries transmit all of the information they receive.'),
        ('虛擬資產轉移資料如果欠缺，必須盡快索取；取不到，便要考慮限制或終止與該機構的關係，或採取合理的風險緩解措施。如果已知資料不完整或沒有意義，同樣須盡快減低風險。另外，持有金錢服務牌照，並不等於已獲准經營虛擬資產交易所。', 'If information for a virtual-asset transfer is missing, it must be obtained promptly. If it cannot be obtained, consider restricting or terminating the relationship with that institution, or take reasonable risk-mitigation measures. Known incomplete or meaningless information also requires prompt mitigation. An MSO licence does not, by itself, authorize the operation of a VA exchange.'),
    ], [
        ref('04', '附表2第11、13A、14條；附表3B', 'Schedule 2 ss.11, 13A, 14; Schedule 3B', 'Special requirements for virtual asset transfer'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('參考：其他行業的附表如何配對', 'Reference: pairing the other sector schedules', [
        ('條例後面的附表3A至3G，是其他行業用的，不要誤當成金錢服務經營者的半年申報。附表3A是 TCSP 費用；3B 界定虛擬資產服務；3C 是其費用；3D 是相聯實體的通知資料；3E 是周年申報資料；3F 是財務報表及核數師報告；3G 是2023年開始的虛擬資產過渡安排。它們各有適用對象。這些「周年申報」並不是第15份文件裡金錢服務經營者的半年申報。', 'Schedules 3A to 3G in the Ordinance belong to other sectors. Do not mistake them for an MSO’s half-yearly return. Schedule 3A contains TCSP fees; 3B defines VA services; 3C contains VA fees; 3D associated-entity notifications; 3E annual-return information; 3F financial statements and auditor reports; and 3G VA transitional arrangements beginning in 2023. Each has its own subject. These annual returns are not the MSO half-yearly returns in document 15.'),
        ('附表3H至3K則是貴金屬及寶石交易商用的。3H 和 3I 分別訂明指明現金交易和指明非現金交易的港幣120,000元門檻。3J 列明非香港交易商現金報告所需資料：交易商及客戶基本資料、相關個人出入境資料，以及交易日期、貨品、現金金額和地點。3K 是 DPMS 費用。這些制度何時適用，見第2部分末節「其他行業制度與 MSO 的界線」。費用細目及已經過了啟動期的過渡程序，保留原文查考，不當作金錢服務經營者日常必背的清單。', 'Schedules 3H to 3K are for dealers in precious metals and stones. Schedules 3H and 3I set the HK$120,000 DPMS cash and non-cash thresholds. Schedule 3J requires basic dealer and customer information, specified individuals’ travel details, and the transaction date, goods, cash amount and location. Schedule 3K contains DPMS fees. See the final Part 2 section, on other sector regimes, for when these apply. Itemised fees, and transition procedures whose commencement periods have passed, remain source references. They are not a daily MSO memorisation list.'),
    ], [
        ref('04', '附表3A–3K；第2部分筆記末節', 'Schedules 3A–3K; Part 2 notes, final section', 'Information to be Provided in Cash Transaction Report'),
    ], kind='reference'),
    block('參考：附表2何時適用於其他行業', 'Reference: when Schedule 2 applies to other sectors', [
        ('保險業甚麼時候要適用附表2，要看業務種類，不是所有一般保險都自動適用同一範圍。就獲授權保險人，section 5(2) 只適用於長期業務。就保險代理、代理機構或經紀公司，section 5(3) 只適用於涉及《保險業條例》附表1第2部第3欄所述長期業務保險合約的交易。', 'When Schedule 2 applies to insurance depends on the type of business. It does not automatically apply to all general insurance in the same way. Section 5(2) applies Schedule 2 to an authorized insurer only for long-term business. Section 5(3) applies it to agents, agencies or broker companies only for transactions involving insurance contracts described in column 3 of Part 2 of Schedule 1 to the Insurance Ordinance (long-term business).'),
        ('儲值支付工具的發行，是否適用附表2，有一條雙重界線，而且剛好港幣3,000元並未達到門檻。section 5(4) 的條件必須同時成立：可儲存的最高價值超過港幣3,000元；而且屬發行人提供予使用者的實物裝置，價值儲存在該裝置上。這只是該條對「發行」的適用界線，並不表示其他電子錢包完全不受監管。例如：一張儲值卡最高只可存港幣3,000元，便不符合「超過3,000元」這項條件，不能只看它是實物裝置就當成已經適用該條。', 'Whether Schedule 2 applies to the issuance of a stored value facility has a two-part boundary, and exactly HK$3,000 does not meet the threshold. Section 5(4) requires both that the maximum value that can be stored is more than HK$3,000, and that the product is a physical device supplied by the issuer to the user, with the value stored on that device. This is the section’s issuance boundary, not a statement that other electronic wallets are wholly unregulated. For example: a stored-value card whose maximum stored value is exactly HK$3,000 does not satisfy the “more than HK$3,000” limb. The fact that it is a physical device is not enough, by itself, to bring the section into play.'),
        ('會計或法律專業人士，不是所有日常工作都會自動適用這套規定。只有在香港以業務形式，為客戶擬備或進行涉及以下一項或以上的交易時，才適用 section 5A(3)：買賣地產；管理客戶款項、證券或其他資產；管理銀行、儲蓄或證券戶口；為成立、營運或管理法團組織資金；成立、營運或管理法人或法律安排；買賣業務實體；或法定信託或公司服務。完整的服務類別，見第2部分末節。', 'Accounting or legal professionals are not brought under these rules by every day-to-day task. Section 5A(3) applies when, by way of business in Hong Kong, they prepare or carry out for a client transactions involving one or more of: buying or selling real estate; managing client money, securities or other assets; managing bank, savings or securities accounts; organising contributions to create, operate or manage corporations; creating, operating or managing legal persons or arrangements; buying or selling business entities; or statutory trust or company services. The complete service categories are in the final Part 2 section.'),
        ('地產代理和 TCSP 持牌人也各有自己的適用範圍。地產代理：在香港涉及為客戶買賣地產的交易，不是概括所有租賃。TCSP 持牌人：以業務形式在香港為客戶擬備或進行法定信託或公司服務交易。就以上會計、法律、地產及 TCSP 的情況，交易標的在香港還是在境外，並無關重要。', 'Estate agents and TCSP licensees each have their own scope. Estate agents are covered where they are involved in Hong Kong in a client’s purchase or sale of real estate, not in every tenancy. TCSP licensees are covered when they prepare or carry out client transactions concerning statutory trust or company services, by way of business in Hong Kong. For these accounting, legal, estate-agent and TCSP cases, it does not matter whether the subject matter of the transaction is in Hong Kong or elsewhere.'),
        ('貴金屬及寶石 B 類註冊人，只有在香港以業務形式與客戶進行非豁除的指明現金交易時，才適用 section 5A(5A)。就付款的 B 類註冊人而言，豁除必須同時符合兩項：現金付款純粹由該 B 類付予另一 B 類；而且交易只有這兩名 B 類當事人。不能把收款方，或任何兩家交易商之間的交易，都一概當成已經豁除。A／B 註冊及現金門檻，見第2部分。', 'For a Category B precious-metals and stones registrant, section 5A(5A) applies only to non-excluded specified cash transactions with a customer, carried on by way of business in Hong Kong. For the paying Category B registrant, exclusion requires both that the cash payments are made exclusively by that registrant to another Category B registrant, and that those two registrants are the only parties to the transaction. Do not automatically exempt the recipient, or every transaction between two dealers. See Part 2 for the registration categories and the cash thresholds.'),
    ], [
        ref('04', '第5(2)–(4)、5A(2)–(7)條；附表1第1部第1條', 'ss.5(2)–(4), 5A(2)–(7); Schedule 1 Part 1 s.1', 'maximum value that can be stored'),
    ], kind='reference'),
]),
section('ongoing-and-records', '持續監察、中介人及紀錄責任', 'Monitoring, intermediaries and records', [
    block('不能把責任外判掉', 'Responsibility remains with the institution', [
        ('持續監察不是「開戶時做完便了事」，而且政治人物、遙距及其他高風險情況還要有額外監察。須定期覆核客戶資料，審視交易是否與背景、業務、風險及資金來源一致，並識別及以書面審查複雜、異常大額或異常模式、而且沒有明顯經濟或合法目的的交易。section 5(4) 及 (5) 分別保留認可數碼識別，以及經適當評估不屬高風險的前政治人物例外；即使如此，一般盡職審查及監察仍然適用。', 'Ongoing monitoring is not finished once the account has been opened. PEP, remote and other high-risk cases also require additional monitoring. Review customer information, scrutinize consistency with background/business/risk and funds sources, and identify/examine in writing complex, unusually large/patterned transactions without apparent economic/lawful purpose. Sections 5(4) and (5) preserve the recognized-digital-ID exception and the exception for former PEPs appropriately assessed as not high-risk, respectively. Ordinary CDD and monitoring still apply.'),
        ('對金錢服務經營者來說，「原有客戶」有一個固定日期，不是永久豁免盡職審查。原有客戶是指在2012年4月1日前已經建立關係的人。出現異常或可疑、或與背景不符的交易、帳戶運作有重大改變、產生懷疑，或對資料有疑問時，便會觸發盡職審查。若無法完成，須盡快終止關係。例如：一名2011年已經往來的顧客，今天突然作出與過往模式明顯不符的大額匯款，仍須補做盡職審查，不能以「是原有客戶」為理由一直不做。', 'For an MSO, “pre-existing customer” is tied to a fixed date. It is not a permanent exemption from CDD. For MSOs, pre-existing customers are those whose relationship was established before 1 April 2012. Unusual or suspicious transactions, transactions inconsistent with the customer’s background, material changes in account operation, suspicion, and doubts about the information, all trigger CDD. If CDD cannot be completed, the relationship must be terminated promptly. For example: a customer who has dealt with the firm since 2011 now makes a large remittance that is clearly inconsistent with the previous pattern. CDD must still be carried out. Pre-existing status is not a reason to leave it undone indefinitely.'),
        ('可以依賴合資格中介人去做部分盡職審查，但責任並不會因此轉走，持續監察仍由金錢服務經營者自己負責。合資格中介人必須書面同意，並能應要求無延誤地提供紀錄。盡職審查資料須在完成後立即取得；支持文件則可在提出要求後，在合理切實可行的範圍內盡快取得。依賴中介人或代理，並不會把本機構的違規責任移轉出去。例如：你請一間合資格中介人核實客戶身分，後來發現核實不足，不能只說「那是中介人的錯」。本機構仍然要負違規責任，持續監察也不能交給中介人便算完成。', 'You may rely on a qualifying intermediary for part of CDD, but liability does not move with that reliance, and ongoing monitoring remains the MSO’s own duty. A qualifying intermediary consents in writing and can supply records without delay on request. Obtain the CDD information immediately after it has been performed. Supporting copies may follow as soon as reasonably practicable after a request. Reliance on an intermediary or an agent does not transfer liability. For example: if you ask a qualifying intermediary to verify a customer’s identity and the verification later turns out to be inadequate, it is not an answer to say “that was the intermediary’s fault”. The institution remains liable for the contravention, and ongoing monitoring is not completed merely by handing it to the intermediary.'),
        ('備存紀錄的「至少5年」，起算日因紀錄種類而不同，不要一律從開戶日起計。客戶、實益擁有人及相關盡職審查紀錄：在關係持續期間備存，並在關係終止後至少再保存5年。非經常交易的相關盡職審查資料，從交易完成後至少保存5年。交易紀錄從交易完成後至少保存5年，而且須可重組該筆交易，並能迅速應監管要求提供。有關當局可以指定更長的保存期。例如：一項2018年已完成的非經常匯款，其盡職審查資料至少要保存到2023年該交易完成日之後；不能因為顧客只來過一次，就在次年把檔案銷毀。', 'The “at least five years” retention period does not all run from the day the account was opened. The starting point depends on the type of record. CDD, customer and beneficial-owner records are kept throughout the relationship, and for at least five years after it ends. Occasional-transaction CDD records are kept for at least five years after the transaction is completed. Transaction records are also kept for at least five years after completion, must allow the transaction to be reconstructed, and must be capable of being produced promptly to the supervisor. The relevant authority may require a longer period. For example: the CDD records for an occasional remittance completed in 2018 must be kept for at least five years after that completion date, into 2023. The file cannot be destroyed the next year merely because the customer only came once.'),
        ('機構還須建立有效的程序，涵蓋政治人物、轉賬資料欠缺，以及各類客戶、產品和交易。在香港成立，或遷冊來港的金融機構，其在海外經營相同業務的分行或附屬公司，須在當地法律容許下實施相若制度；如果不能實施，須通知有關當局，並另作緩解。', 'An institution must also maintain effective procedures covering PEPs, deficient transfer information, and its various customers, products and transactions. Hong Kong-incorporated or re-domiciled financial institutions apply similar systems in overseas same-business branches/subsidiaries where local law permits; notify the authority and mitigate where not possible.'),
    ], [
        ref('04', '附表2第5–6、18–23條', 'Schedule 2 ss.5–6, 18–23', 'occasional transaction is completed'),
    ], kind='list'),
]),
section('fees', '附表3：金錢服務牌照費用', 'Schedule 3: MSO licensing fees', [
    block('按repo所存2026年綜合版本', 'Amounts in the repo’s 2026 consolidated edition', [
        ('附表3的金錢服務牌照費用，要分開「新牌」和「續牌」，也要分開基本費、額外處所費和適當人選評核費。新牌申請：基本港幣3,810元，另每個額外營業處所港幣2,440元，每名須作適當人選評核的人港幣945元。續牌：基本港幣910元，另每個額外處所港幣410元，每名評核人士同樣是港幣945元。這些是所存2026年綜合版本的數額，實際申請須核對當時的法定費表。', 'Schedule 3 MSO fees need to be separated into grant and renewal, and then into the base fee, the additional-premises fee and the fit-and-proper fee. Grant application: HK$3,810 base, plus HK$2,440 per additional business premises and HK$945 per person subject to the fit-and-proper test. Renewal: HK$910 base, plus HK$410 per additional premises and HK$945 per tested person. These are the amounts in the stored 2026 consolidated edition. An actual application requires the then-current statutory fee schedule.'),
        ('人事或處所變動的申請，也有獨立收費。申請批准新增董事、最終擁有人或合夥人：每人港幣945元。申請加入新營業處所，或由沒有特定處所改為在特定處所經營：每個處所港幣2,440元。', 'Applications to change people or premises have their own fees. Approval applications for directors, ultimate owners or partners cost HK$945 per person. Adding premises, or applying to operate at particular premises, costs HK$2,440 per premises.'),
        ('查閱登記冊是免費的，但索取副本或證明書要收費，兩件事不要混為一談。核證登記冊副本或摘錄，每份港幣160元；非核證副本每頁或不足一頁港幣1.5元；section 28(1)(b) 的證明書每份港幣160元。這些同樣只是所存版本的數額，實際申請須核對當時表格及法定費表。', 'Public inspection of the register is free, but copies and certificates are charged for, and the two should not be mixed up. Certified register copies or extracts cost HK$160 each; uncertified copies cost HK$1.50 per page or part-page; and section 28(1)(b) certificates cost HK$160 each. These too are stored-edition amounts. Actual applications require the then-current form and statutory fee schedule.'),
    ], [
        ref('04', '第27–28條；附表3', 'ss.27–28; Schedule 3', '3,810'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('申請費、適當人選測試費與退費', 'Application fees, fitness-test fees and refunds', [
        ('申請費和適當人選測試費，不論其後是批准還是拒絕，都不退還。每名受適當人選測試的人士須繳港幣945元，批牌時要繳，每次續牌也要再繳，不是整家公司只付一次。例如：一間公司有三名董事都要接受適當人選測試，續牌時不是只付一筆945元，而是三個人各付945元；即使續牌最後被拒，已繳費用也不會退回。', 'Application fees, and the fit-and-proper test fee, are non-refundable whether the application is approved or refused. HK$945 is payable for each person subject to the fit-and-proper test, at grant and again at every renewal, not once for the whole company. For example: a company with three directors who are all subject to the test does not pay a single HK$945 at renewal. It pays HK$945 for each of the three persons. If the renewal is later refused, the fees already paid are still not refunded.'),
    ], [
        ref('05', '第2.8、4.13–4.14、6.3段', '¶2.8, 4.13–4.14, 6.3', 'fee paid for the fit and proper person test is non'),
        ref('04', '附表3第4–5項', 'Schedule 3 items 4–5', 'plus for each person who is subject to the fit'),
    ], kind='list'),
]),
section('tribunal-schedule', '附表4：審裁處成員及聆訊安排', 'Schedule 4: tribunal membership and hearings', [
    block('成員、表決及出席', 'Membership, voting and attendance', [
        ('審裁處怎樣組成，先要記主席的資格和委員團的產生方法。主席必須具有獲委任為高等法院法官的資格，而且除了審裁處主席等法定例外外，不是公職人員。主席任期不超過3年，可以續任。局長另外委任非公職人員組成委員團，並依主席建議，為每一宗覆核選出兩名普通成員。', 'The composition of the tribunal starts with the chair’s qualifications and the way the panel is formed. The chair must be qualified for appointment as a judge of the High Court, and must not be a public officer except for the statutory exceptions such as holding office as the tribunal chair. The term is up to three years, and may be renewed. The Secretary appoints a panel of persons who are not public officers, and, on the chair’s recommendation, two ordinary members are selected for each review.'),
        ('聆訊通常要主席連同兩名普通成員在席，以多數票決定；但法律問題由主席單獨決定。如果主席的任期在案件中途屆滿，他可以繼續把該案審完。若成員中途變更，必須得到各方同意才可以繼續；否則程序中止，但可以重新開始。', 'A hearing normally requires the chair and two ordinary members to sit, and they decide by majority. Questions of law, however, are decided by the chair alone. If the chair’s term expires in the middle of a review, the chair may finish that review. If the membership changes, the proceedings may continue only with the parties’ consent; otherwise they are discontinued, but they may be started again.'),
        ('聆訊一般公開進行；但為了司法公正，審裁處可以依職權或因申請而決定不公開，而申請不公開本身的聆訊也是不公開的。各方可以親自出席；公司可由高級人員或僱員出席，合夥可由合夥人出席，當局可由代表出席。各方也有權由律師或大律師代表；如果要由其他人代表，則須取得審裁處許可。', 'Hearings are normally held in public. In the interests of justice, the tribunal may sit in private, either on its own initiative or on an application, and the hearing of an application for privacy is itself held in private. Parties may attend in person. A corporation may attend through an officer or employee, a partnership through a partner, and an authority through a representative. Parties are entitled to be represented by a solicitor or counsel. Representation by any other person requires the tribunal’s leave.'),
    ], [
        ref('04', '第56條；附表4第2–6條', 's.56; Schedule 4 ss.2–6', 'a question of law is to be determined by the chairperson alone'),
    ], kind='list'),
    block('初步會議、同意命令及主席單獨處理', 'Preliminary conferences, consent orders and chair alone', [
        ('正式審理前可以用初步會議和同意命令，但兩者都必須得到各方同意。初步會議須各方同意，目的是協助準備、釐清爭點，並以公正、迅速和節省費用的方式處理覆核；由主席主持，並向審裁處報告。同意命令必須由各方要求，並且同意全部條款，而且必須是審裁處或主席本來就有權作出的命令。', 'Before the main hearing, a preliminary conference or a consent order may be used, but both require the parties’ agreement. Preliminary conferences need the parties’ agreement, and are used to prepare and clarify issues so that the review can be dealt with justly, expeditiously and economically. The chair presides and reports to the tribunal. A consent order requires a request from the parties and their agreement to all of its terms, and it must be an order that the tribunal or the chair already has power to make.'),
        ('在某些情況下，主席可以獨自處理，不必等到全體成員在席。正式審理開始前，若各方書面同意，可由主席作為唯一成員裁定該宗覆核。延長申請覆核期限，以及暫緩指明決定的申請，也可以由主席單獨處理。如果主席不能或不適宜處理暫緩申請，終審法院首席法官可以委任原訟法庭法官或暫委法官代行。', 'In some situations the chair may sit alone, without waiting for the full membership. Before the determination hearing, the parties may agree in writing that the chair alone should decide the review. The chair may also determine, sitting alone, an application to extend the time for applying for review, and an application for a stay of a specified decision. If the chair is unable or unsuited to deal with the stay application, the Chief Justice may appoint a Court of First Instance judge or a deputy judge to act instead.'),
    ], [
        ref('04', '附表4第7–9條', 'Schedule 4 ss.7–9', 'Preliminary conferences'),
    ], kind='list'),
]),
])
